{
 "metadata": {
  "name": "Motor-EPM \u00b7 CORRIDOR \u00b7 GRAVITY-REFERENCED FOOT SENSE (oracle removed)",
  "description": "The reward-free stack with the GOD'S-EYE swing signal REMOVED. feet_topic now reads reality.proprio.feet_y_gravity = encoder-FK foot position projected onto the accelerometer's gravity-up axis (IK + IMU) \u2014 instead of feet_y, which was absolute WORLD-Y and which no real picrawler can sense. Three earlier legal replacements all LOST badly (body-frame FK 2.52, FK+belly-ToF 2.26, true foot contact 2.37 vs the oracle's 3.76) and two phase hypotheses died at chance agreement; the property they all lacked was a GRAVITY reference, which is exactly what an accelerometer provides. RESULT n=4: net_z 3.76->3.95, and flat_v 0.04->0.05 \u2014 the FIRST movement in flat speed across 10+ levers. Leg participation improves markedly (step_bal 0.25->0.42, steps 74->113). Hump gate PASSES and improves (final_z 5.21->5.35, gain_z 2.59->2.75, 0 falls). COSTS: straightness 0.70->0.62 and wobble tilt_sd 0.067->0.095 \u2014 livelier but less controlled. HARDWARE NOTE: buildable on the real robot, but hobby servos do not report position, so real FK would use COMMANDED angles (blind to load deflection) and real attitude needs gyro/accel fusion (a bare accelerometer confuses gravity with body acceleration). Both gaps are untested. gym_mode=corridor.",
